  m_Name: Cleidobrachial_muscle_Clavicular_part_of_deltoid.L
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ModelPartDataSO
  id: Cleidobrachial_muscle_Clavicular_part_of_deltoid.L
  partName: Cleidobrachial_muscle_Clavicular_part_of_deltoid.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The cleidobrachial muscle is part of the brachiocephalicus group and primarily
    functions to extend the forelimb forward. It plays a crucial role in locomotion
    by advancing the limb in a controlled and coordinated manner during walking and
    running. Additionally, it helps stabilize the shoulder joint, preventing excessive
    movement. '
  - This muscle works in conjunction with neck and shoulder muscles to maintain smooth,
    rhythmic motion and contributes significantly to stride length, balance, and
    efficient forward propulsion during dynamic activities.
